# The substation reference from plan/00-foundation/01-vision-and-scope.md.
#
# Two hydraulic circuits coupled only through HX1: heat crosses, fluid does not. The primary is open
# and states both its pressures; the secondary is a closed loop and gets an auto-picked datum
# (FS2201). Sharing HX1 is what stops either side being reported as an isolated subgraph -- D-17.
#
# `dn` is stated on every pipe because the catalogue that would supply it lands in P3.5.

fluidscript 1
circuit substation
fluid water
show temperature

# --- district-heating primary, 85/45 -------------------------------
NPS node t=85 p=600
NPR node p=350
PCV valve
PP  pipe length=12 dn=25

# --- heating secondary, 40/60 --------------------------------------
SP   pump
SS   pipe length=30 dn=32
SR   pipe length=30 dn=32
LOAD heat_exchanger power=-150 dt=20

# --- the exchanger between them ------------------------------------
HX1 heat_exchanger power=150 in=40 out=60 in2=85 out2=45 u=3300

connections
NPS - PCV - PP - HX1.in2
HX1.out2 - NPR

HX1.out - SS - NSUP
NSUP - LOAD - NRET
NRET - SR - SP - HX1.in
